/// The Terms of Service and Privacy Policy, as data.
///
/// One source for three readers: the in-app pages (`auth/presentation/
/// legal_screen.dart`), the vault's canonical Markdown (regenerated by
/// `dart run tool/export_legal.dart`), and — once the web app has its
/// `/terms` and `/privacy` routes — the site. Edit the text here, bump the
/// version and date, re-run the export. Never edit the Markdown by hand.
///
/// Pure Dart on purpose (no Flutter import), so the export tool can run it
/// with `dart run`.
///
/// What the law asks of these pages, and where each requirement is met, is
/// in the vault: `01 - Product/Legal/`. In short — DPDP Act 2023 s.5 notice
/// (itemised data, purposes, how to exercise rights, how to complain to the
/// Board), s.6 consent by clear affirmative action (the signup checkbox),
/// s.8(9) a published contact for questions, s.11–14 rights; DPDP Rules 2025
/// r.3 (notice stands alone, plain language), r.9 (contact), r.14 (how to
/// make a request); IT Act s.43A SPDI Rules 2011 r.4 (what a privacy policy
/// must contain) and r.5(9) (a named Grievance Officer, one-month
/// resolution); Apple guideline 5.1.1 (retention/deletion and how to revoke
/// consent must be stated; the link must be reachable in the app).
library;

